    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3992\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to rules relating to\nthe processing of health claims and overpayments to physicians and\nother health care providers\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo set forth a number of reforms to the manner by which health\ninsurance companies process claims for health insurance benefits from\nhealth care providers.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill amends section 3224-b(b) of the Insurance Law by expanding\nthe existing statute to cover all health care providers.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nCurrently, section 3224-b(b) of the Insurance Law applies only to\nphysicians and provides that when insurance overpayments occur, a\nhealth plan shall provide thirty days written notice before seeking\nrecovery of the overpayment of claims, and a health plan shall not\ninitiate overpayment recovery efforts more than twenty-four months\nafter the original payment was received. This bill would make these\nprovisions applicable to other health care providers.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation seeks to address some of the difficulties faced by\nhealth care providers when dealing with health insurance plans. In\n2006, legislation was signed into law as Chapter 551 that amended the\nrules relating to the processing of health claims and overpayments to\nphysicians.  This legislation would expand the 2006 law to make the\nrules relating to the processing of health claims and overpayments\napply to all health care providers. This legislation would establish\nfair, uniform and consistent procedures for the processing of\noverpayment recovery claims for all health care providers.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis law would take effect January 1, 2010 and shall apply to health\ncare claims submitted for payment after such date.\n",
